{
  "name": "4-speed compound gearbox",
  "note": "Two shifting stages in series. One pair of shafts can only give two shifted ratios -- every pair on it sums to the same tooth count, and only 16t and 20t come as clutch gears -- so four speeds means two stages. The stages are set two studs and two and a half studs apart so their ratios differ: 0.60 and 1.00 against 1.50 and 1.00, which multiply out to four distinct speeds rather than three.",
